record lows","records":"Pine Bluff has nearly stopped setting record lows","change":"Pine Bluff's nights have warmed. Its days cooled over the long run but have warmed since 1983.","rain":"Rain and snow: no clear long-term change"},"text":{"lede":"Yesterday's high of 56\u00b0F was the 26th coolest November 13 high (tied) of 136 since 1889, the coolest since 2022.","t_yest":"November 13: cooler than 81% of years","p_yest":"The high of <strong>56\u00b0F</strong> was the 26th coolest November 13 high (tied) of 136 since 1889, the coolest since 2022. The normal high for the date is 64\u00b0F, and the record is 87\u00b0F (1955). The low of <strong>34\u00b0F</strong> was typical for November 13.","t_rec":"Pine Bluff has nearly stopped setting record lows","p_rec":"If Pine Bluff's climate weren't changing, every year would have the same chance of holding a daily record. Since 2000, Pine Bluff has set <strong class=\"sig\">35 standing record lows</strong>, far fewer than the 72 that chance alone would give, and <strong>42 record highs</strong>, fewer than the 72 that chance alone would give. The 1920s hold the most record highs of any decade (88). Pine Bluff's all-time high is 112\u00b0F, on August 15, 1943.","t_chg":"Pine Bluff's nights have warmed. Its days cooled over the long run but have warmed since 1983.","p_chg":"Across 124 complete years: Pine Bluff's average low has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.14\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.07 to +0.22), about +1.9\u00b0F since 1892. Pine Bluff's average high has fallen <strong class='sig'>\u22120.17\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range \u22120.24 to \u22120.09), about \u22122.2\u00b0F since 1892. <strong>The last 40 years tell a different story:</strong> since 1983, lows have risen <strong class='sig'>+0.46\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.07 to +0.85) and highs have risen <strong class='sig'>+0.55\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.17 to +0.94). The full record joins different observing sites over the years, and a move (for example, from the city to a cooler airport) can hide or exaggerate a long-run trend, so the recent decades are the clearer guide here.","t_mon":"Lows rose in 7 of 12 months. Highs rose in none; 3 months fell.","t_rain":"Rain and snow: no clear long-term change","p_rain":"Pine Bluff's yearly precipitation shows no clear long-term change (\u22120.10 inches per decade, a range that includes zero). The 1991\u20132020 normal is 50.1 inches a year. The wettest year was 1905 (82.89 in); the driest, 2010 (28.43 in).","show_snow":true,"sig_bars":{"lo":true,"hi":false},"t_year":"2026 so far: 8 daily record highs, no daily record lows"}}